<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">German occupation of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The German occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> began in 1943, after Italy signed an armistice with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and German forces took control of much of the country. It followed the collapse of the Fascist regime and the loss of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>'s colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy.jpg" alt="German occupation of Italy" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rieder, Fred · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-J15358,_Bozen,_entwaffneten_Badoglio-Einheiten_marschieren_durch_die_Stadt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
